  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only multiprofile models with scVI_n200 and avgpool/transformer aggregation reach about 0.65 validation accuracy, clearly above PCA-based RNA models, weak image-only ResNet baselines, and the one tested multimodal ResNet concat configuration. The main remaining uncertainty in this promising RNA direction is whether another learned RNA encoder, scGPT, can match or improve scVI_n200. config_008 keeps the proven multiprofile avgpool setting and changes only the RNA encoder, making it a clean test of representation quality. This is the best next experiment because it targets the dominant modality, has high expected immediate performance, and reduces uncertainty about RNA encoder choice before investing further in image or fusion variants."
}

